<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The mod's own recreation type, alongside Core's Gaming_Dexterity and Gaming_Cerebral. It is
    what makes the console worth building next to a chess table: joy tolerance is tracked per
    kind, so a colony that only plays cerebral games gets diminishing returns from them, and
    video gaming is a fresh column.

    A kind with nothing to satisfy it costs the colony nothing. Tolerance is only ever raised by
    JoyToleranceSet.Notify_JoyGained, which is reached by actually doing the activity, and the
    boredom alert asks whether a pawn is bored of the kinds *available* on the map. The one
    visible effect of an unsatisfied kind is a line of text: JoyUtility.JoyKindsNotOnMapString
    lists it among the recreation types the map does not offer, exactly as vanilla lists
    telescope study on a colony with no telescope.
  -->

  <JoyKindDef>
    <defName>Gaming_Video</defName>
    <label>video gaming</label>
  </JoyKindDef>

</Defs>
